Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 20:59:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08103/11362] The gate is silent exactly where it is needed:
 content failures eat the attempts it runs on

Found in the live A/B's first treatment cell, not in review. ar25 accepted a textbook
`return False` -- the model's own comment reads "no win state was given ... maybe just return
False" -- with goal_defect_reasks == 0 AND engine_defect_reasks == 0. Both gates silent at once
is what pointed at a shared cause rather than a bug in the new one.

`attempt < tries - 1` guards both defect gates. It exists for a good reason: a `continue` on the
last attempt would fall out of the loop and convert an accept into a hard failure. The side
effect is that every attempt the model spends on a CONTENT failure -- no code block, missing
`def`, a syntax error -- consumes an attempt the defect gate needed, and an answer accepted on
the final attempt is never checked at all.

So the gate is quietest exactly where it is most needed. A game the model finds hard burns its
attempts on malformed output, then lands its one parseable answer on the attempt where nothing
is armed. Confirmed offline against a scripted server: accepted on attempt 0 gives 2 re-asks;
two content failures then the SAME defective answer gives 0, accepted unchecked.

THIS IS NOT A REGRESSION FROM THE GOAL GATE. The shipped ENGINE gate carries the identical
guard and the identical blind spot, so its measured 13/36 -> 22/36 is a FLOOR on what that gate
could do, not a ceiling.

NOT FIXED MID-RUN, deliberately. The fix -- attempts the defect gates own, which content
failures cannot consume -- is a behaviour change to shipped code, and applying it while the A/B
was in flight would have measured two different treatments under one label. Recommended
follow-up, recorded with the incident that motivates it.

Effect on the measurement in flight, stated now rather than discovered in the write-up: the
treatment is WEAKER than designed, so a null must be read as "this weakened treatment did not
move the primary", never as "goal re-asking does not help". The armedness block reports the
realised firing rate against the 94.8% that were detectable; the gap between those two numbers
IS this blind spot, measured.

